<!-- The D. Idaho complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the
     typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; Loc. Civ. R. 5.2(a) names no face and asks at least 12 point, footer
     included; size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 27.6 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double; LR 5.2(a)
     double-spaced) with a half-inch indent, and the headings in them, with no space of their own; the counsel,
     caption, signature and footer lines in 13.8 pt boxes (typst pitch-single); letter page with 1-inch margins
     (LR 5.2(a)). docx/idd-complaint.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing, the footer (the page number and the
     paper's title, LR 5.2(a), its line 36.75 pt above the page foot: 735 twips, where typst sets it, footer-descent
     30 %) and the last section. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
